      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:139:6",
      "text": [
        " إِنَّ أَوَّلَ مَنْ يُكَذِّبُ الْكَذَّابَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ ثُمَّ الْمَلَكَانِ اللَّذَانِ مَعَهُ ثُمَّ هُوَ يَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ كَاذِبٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Ali Bin Al Hakam, from Aban Al Ahmar, from Fuzayl Bin Yasaar, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The first one to belie the liar is Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic. Then it is the two (Recording) Angels who are with him. Then he (himself) knows that he is a liar’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Ali ibn al-Hakam from Aban al-Ahmar from Fudayl ibn Yasar from abu Ja’far (a.s.) who has said the following: “Abu Ja’far (a.s.) has said, ‘The first one to rebuff the liar is Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most Holy, then the two angels who are with him, then he is the one who knows he is a liar.’” "
        ]
      }
